  WHAT IS ACTUALLY DERIVED FROM BLENDER

  1. One file is a literal port of Blender source:

       src/boolean_predicates.rs
         from:      source/blender/blenlib/BLI_math_boolean.hh
                    source/blender/blenlib/intern/math_boolean.cc
         commit:    96294be75080bbf687fa7f108e344a1063713586
         copyright: SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2023 Blender Authors
         licence:   SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

     Only the `double` (floating-point) predicate API is ported; Blender's
     `mpq_class` (GMP rational) overloads are deliberately not, so this crate
     stays Android-buildable with no C dependencies. Blender's own `double`
     predicates are in turn a C++ adaptation of Jonathan Richard Shewchuk's
     `predicates.c` (Carnegie Mellon University, May 1996), which its author
     placed in the public domain. The file carries this provenance in its own
     header block; do not strip it during refactors.

  2. Everything else is an independent reimplementation of Blender's
     mesh/geometry ARCHITECTURE -- the shape of the BMesh-style non-manifold
     mesh representation (vert/edge/loop/face) and the modifier/operator model,
     including its naming. No Blender code is transcribed in those files.
     Copyright covers expression, not design.

